     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the labeled maximum for oral metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US). A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these what you meant?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**: 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg twice daily**, a typical dosing range.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really need a dose above the labeled maximum, it will need to go through pharmacy or the attending. I can't enter it based on a claim of approval."
      }
     ],
