       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. I have no way to verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and the dose is still 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum. Confirming it doesn't change that.\n\nHere's what you can do:\n- **Pharmacy or attending review:** if a clinician wants a dose above the label, they can go through the hospital's process for exceeding maximum doses. That usually means pharmacy verification and a documented override.\n- **Enter a dose within the label now:** I can enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) so the patient isn't left without therapy while that's sorted out.\n- **Other options:** if standard metformin dosing has failed, the specialist may prefer adding or switching to another agent. I can enter that order if you give me the drug and dose.\n\nTell me which of these you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
